-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/1355b147-caed-5c94-8d86-7674a3fcf72c
-- title:
--   Level automorphisms moving the ∞-Igusa ring decentre good points (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to the hypothesis `hq2` that $q = 2$, and $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`). Write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Two geometric function fields inside the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the image under coefficientwise extension `coeffEmb` of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself the $\mathbb Q$-field generated by the divisor expansions of level $M'$), and `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. Furthermore $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; `ResidueField A` is its residue field and `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` the field generated over it by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $M'$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` is given, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places $w$ that are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of $j$-values all of whose elliptic curves have no non-zero $q$-torsion affine point.
--
--   Reduction data. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the geometric level-$M'$ field, a ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto the reduced field, and a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, subject to the structure's axioms (constants lie in `R₀.integers` precisely when they lie in $A$; the residue map is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal and is compatible with the residue map of $A$; every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant into `R₀.integers` with non-zero residue; `placeMap` preserves degrees and is compatible with divisors of functions). The hypothesis `hR₀` pins this down coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue`, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Igusa data. $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$, and `OSS` assigns one to each $s \in W$. Four hypotheses concern `OIg`: `hIg_inf` identifies `OIg (lineInfty q)` (the line through $(1,0)$) as the Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it exactly when there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the reduction of $y$ is non-zero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$; `hIg` says that every line $\ell$ is reached from `lineInfty q` by `redQ q γ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says `OIg` is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`, i.e. there is a permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line with `(OIg ℓ).comap … = OIg (σ ℓ)` for all $\ell$.
--
--   Supersingular data. Four hypotheses concern `OSS`. `hSS_A`: for each $s$ and each $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in `OSS s` exactly when $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for each $s \in W$ and each $f$ in `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element `coeffEmb`$(\mathtt{jq})$ (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant) has non-negative order, and such that `R₀.residue f` lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{R₀.residue } f)$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in `OSS s` and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each `OSS s` is its own pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: each `OSS s` contains an element $t$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in `OSS s` and is a unit there.
--
--   Prolongation data. $R$ is a `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`, i.e. a valuation subring `R.integers` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced level-$H$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing the residue map of $A$ on constants, with constants in `R.integers` exactly those of $A$ and with every non-zero element scalable into `R.integers` with non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR` identifies `R.integers` with `OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` says that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)`.
--
--   Arithmetic data. An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$ is given. Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian local (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and is residually surjective onto that of $A$ in the form `hκ`: every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Further, $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite-dimensional over $k_0$, and $A_1$ is a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements lying in $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a discrete valuation ring and henselian local.
--
--   Conclusion. With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-field generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-field generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Put $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-field generated by the image of $K_1$ in `fieldBar q M'`. The assertion is further made for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map sends $a \in A_1$ to the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, and for every $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element `coeffEmb`$(\mathtt{jq})$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` included via `hle`, with $j_1 \neq 0$. Let $\mathfrak X$ denote [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (those integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along their common middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$.
--
--   Five predicates are introduced by `let`. For $x \in \mathfrak X$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of the finite chart mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for the chart at infinity with `ιInf` and `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in each case. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation $< 1$ of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ exactly when `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$, and the same for the chart at infinity; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, holds when every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers` with `R.residue f` in the valuation subring of $Q$ and a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`; this abbreviation does not occur in the final conclusion. `OffBranch x` holds when for every line $\ell \neq$ `lineInfty q`, for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$ there is $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `OIg ℓ` with $b \notin y$, and likewise for the chart at infinity.
--
--   The conclusion itself: for every $g$ in the subgroup of the group of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the set of all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, if the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along $g$ differs from `OIg (lineInfty q)`, then for all points $x, x'$ of $\mathfrak X$ with `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x`, `GoodPt x'` and `OffBranch x'`, and for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: if `Centred P x` then `Centred (g • P) x'` fails.
--
--   This is the case $q = 2$ of the separation statement on the Igusa leg of the semistable-covering construction for the full-level modular curve: a product of level automorphisms which does not preserve the Gauss ring attached to the line at infinity cannot carry a place centred at a good point off the other Igusa branches to a place centred at another such point. It is used in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two).
